    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As Hombre (declarer), win at least six of the ten tricks, either alone (Solo) or with a partner (Alliance). Opponents aim to prevent this.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Stakes**: Each player antes to the pool (or dealer antes four). 2. **Auction**: Eldest opens; players bid or pass in ascending order: Solo, Casco (with both black Aces), Dimidiator (exchange with called King), Alliance (call a King for partner). If all pass, Forced Spadille: holder of Spadille becomes Hombre and calls a King. 3. **Trump**: Hombre names trump (or partner may in Forced Spadille). 4. **Play**: Eldest leads. Must follow suit; may play any card if void. Highest trump wins, else highest of led suit. Spadille, Manille, Basta may be held back when trumps are led (unless a higher trump is led). 5. **Settlement**: Hombre wins or loses; pool and premiums paid accordingly.',
      "Scoring example: Stake-based. Hombre wins: takes pool and premiums (Solo, Matadors, Premiers). Hombre loses: Remise (5 tricks) = double pool; Codille (4 or fewer) = stiffer penalty. Bonuses: Premiers (six tricks before opponents take one), Matadors (top trumps held). Hombre (or Hombre's team) wins by taking six or more tricks. Loses with five (Remise) or four or fewer (Codille)..",
